NAME
     env - run a program in a changed environment

SYNOPSIS
     env [-i] [-u NAME] [NAME=VALUE...] [COMMAND [ARG...]]
     printenv [NAME...]

DESCRIPTION
     env runs COMMAND with the environment changed as its arguments say.
     With no COMMAND it prints the environment. Called as printenv it
     prints one variable, or all of them.

OPTIONS
     -i        start from an empty environment
     -u NAME   remove NAME

SEE ALSO
     sh(1), echoenv(1)
